            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to go past, then the Russian for to see off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: регистрация",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "регистрация (registrátsiya) — \"check-in; registration\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Регистрация начинается в шесть утра. Registrátsiya nachináyetsya v shest utrá. Check-in opens at six in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Стойка регистрации — the check-in desk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "регистрация (registrátsiya) is a learned word built on регистр 'a register', usually traced to Medieval Latin registrum 'a list'. EtymDB lists the Russian word without a source, so the line is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
